{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '330,400p' TOPOPILOT_SCRIPTING_GUIDE.txt && sed -n '1,190p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/ui/script_template.py && sed -n '1,270p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/types/pointsTypes.py\"","aggregated_output":"SymmetricTensorMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a symmetric tensor field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nAsymmetricTensorMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts an asymmetric tensor field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nScalarGradient(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a scalar field to its vector gradient field.\n\nVectorGradient(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a vector field to its asymmetric-tensor gradient/Jacobian field.\n\n\nPOINT COMPUTATION AND EMBEDDING\n-------------------------------\n\nComputeScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, which_points)\n    Computes selected critical points of a scalar field. which_points must be one\n    of these exact strings:\n      - \"all critical points (mins+maxes+saddles)\"\n      - \"minima\"\n      - \"maxima\"\n      - \"saddles\"\n      - \"all contour tree vertices (mins+maxes+saddles)\"\n      - \"contour tree saddles\"\n\nComputeVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id)\n    Computes critical points of a vector field.\n\nComputeSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id)\n    Computes degenerate points of a symmetric tensor field.\n\nComputeAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id)\n    Computes degenerate points of an asymmetric tensor field.\n\nEmbedScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                          color_scheme=[\"#3b4cc0\", \"#aac7fd\", \"#f7b89c\",\n                                        \"#b40426\", \"#000000\"])\n    Displays scalar critical points as spheres. radius controls sphere size.\n    color_scheme contains five hex colors for minima, index-1 saddles, index-2\n    saddles, maxima, and degenerate points.\n\nEmbedVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                          color_scheme=[\"#9d2c00\", \"#f0c571\", \"#0b81a2\",\n                                        \"#e25759\", \"#7e4794\", \"#59a89c\"])\n    Displays vector critical points as spheres. The six colors represent sources,\n    saddles, sinks, source spirals, centers, and sink spirals.\n\nEmbedSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                                     color_scheme=[\"#ffffff\", \"#ff8cc6\"])\n    Displays symmetric-tensor degenerate points. The two colors represent\n    trisectors and wedges; radius controls sphere size.\n\nEmbedAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                                      color_scheme=[\"#ffffff\", \"#ff8cc6\"])\n    Displays asymmetric-tensor degenerate points. The two colors represent\n    trisectors and wedges; radius controls sphere size.\n\n\nPOINT TRACKING AND TRACKED-POINT EMBEDDING\n------------------------------------------\n\nTracking requires a time-series root. For each Track... node, time_steps is a\npositive number of steps or -1 for every available step. backend must be \"emd\",\n\"sinkhorn\", or \"partial\".\n\nTrackScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n    Tracks scalar critical points over time.\n\nTrackVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n    Tracks vector critical points over time.\nfrom paraview.simple import *\nfrom topopilot.nodes import *\nimport topopilot.config as config\nimport topopilot.nodeTree as tree\nimport argparse\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nDEFAULT_RANDOM_SEED = 0\n\ndef pipeline(load_path):\n    pass\n\ndef create_view():\n    pass\n\ndef validate_arguments(args):\n    if args.i[-4:] == \".vti\":\n        time_steps = 1\n    else:\n        if not os.path.isdir(args.i):\n            print(\"error: file specified with -i must either be .vti file or directory\")\n            exit(1)\n        \n        time_steps = len(os.listdir(args.i))\n        \n        basename = os.path.basename(args.i)\n        dirname = os.path.dirname(args.i)\n\n        for i in range(1,time_steps+1):\n            \n            if not os.path.isfile(f\"{dirname}/{basename}/{basename}{i}.vti\"):\n                print(\"error: invalid input format for directory\")\n                print(f\"missing file {dirname}/{basename}/{basename}{i}.vti\")\n                exit(1)\n        \n    if args.t > time_steps:\n        print(\"error: time step is too high\")\n        exit(1)                             \n\n    if args.x and args.t == -1 and time_steps > 1:\n        print(\"error: cannot run interactive mode on multiple time steps\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.o != \"\" and args.x:\n        print(\"error: you cannot specify an output file and -interactive\")\n        exit(1)\n    \n    if args.o == \"\" and not args.x:\n        print(\"error: you must either specify an output file or run in interactive mode.\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.t == -1 and time_steps > 1 and args.o[-4:] != \".mp4\":\n        print(\"error: when outputting to video format your output filename must end in .mp4\")\n        exit(1)\n    \n    if args.t != -1 and not args.x and args.o[-4:] != \".png\":\n        print(\"error: when outputting to image format your output filename must end in .png\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.t == -1 and time_steps == 1:\n        args.t = 1\n\n    return time_steps\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"User generated scientific visualization pipeline. Generates images or videos based on user input.\")\n\n    parser.add_argument(\"-i\", help=\"The file that should be loaded.\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-x\", help=\"Should you load into interactive mode? (no images will be generated)\", action=argparse.BooleanOptionalAction)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-o\", help=\"The name of the file that we are outputting.\", default=\"\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"-t\", help=\"What time step should be loaded. Put -1 to generate a video of all time steps. If the data only has one time step, -1 will just load the one time step.\", type=int, default=-1)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-q\", help=\"What folder should be used for temporary files\", default=\".\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--seed\", help=\"Seed for TopoPilot-owned random colors and identifiers.\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_RANDOM_SEED)\n\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    time_steps = validate_arguments(args)\n\n    config.set_random_seed(args.seed)\n    config.change_session_folder(args.q)\n\n    sessionDir = Path(f\"{config.session_folder()}\")\n    sessionDir.mkdir(exist_ok = True)\n    cacheDir = Path(f\"{config.session_folder()}/cache\")\n    cacheDir.mkdir(exist_ok = True)\n\n    nodes_to_visualize, color_bar_info, time_invariant_nodes_to_cache, normal_nodoes_to_cache = pipeline(args.i)\n\n    if args.t != -1:\n\n        renderView = create_view()\n        renderView.Background = [1.0, 1.0, 1.0]\n        renderView.UseColorPaletteForBackground = 0\n\n        for n in nodes_to_visualize:\n            props = n.visualize(args.t, renderView)\n\n            if n.id in color_bar_info:\n                position, length, title = color_bar_info[n.id]\n\n                lut = props.LookupTable\n                bar = GetScalarBar(lut, renderView)\n\n                bar.WindowLocation = \"Any Location\"\n                bar.Position = position\n                bar.ScalarBarLength = length\n                bar.Title = title\n                bar.ComponentTitle = ''\n\n                props.SetScalarBarVisibility(renderView, True)\n\n        if args.o:\n            SaveScreenshot(args.o)\n        else:\n            Interact()\n\n    else:\n\n        for t in range(time_steps):\n\n            renderView = create_view()\n\n            for n in nodes_to_visualize:\n                props = n.visualize(t+1, renderView)\n\n                if n.id in color_bar_info:\n                    position, length, title = color_bar_info[n.id]\n\n                    lut = props.LookupTable\n                    bar = GetScalarBar(lut, renderView)\n\n                    bar.WindowLocation = \"Any Location\"\n                    bar.Position = position\n                    bar.ScalarBarLength = length\n                    bar.Title = title\n                    bar.ComponentTitle = ''\n\n                    props.SetScalarBarVisibility(renderView, True)\n\n            SaveScreenshot(f\"{args.q}/frame{str(t+1).zfill(8)}.png\", renderView)\n\n            Disconnect()\n            tree.clear_evaluation_cache()\n            Connect()\n\n        os.system(f\"ffmpeg -framerate 4 -i {args.q}/frame%08d.png -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p {args.o}\")\n\n        for t in range(time_steps):\n            os.remove(f\"{args.q}/frame{str(t+1).zfill(8)}.png\")\nimport os\n\nfrom .nodeData import NodeData\nfrom paraview.simple import *\nfrom typing_extensions import List\n\nimport topopilot.ttk as ttk\nfrom topopilot.utils import categorical_map_filter\nimport vtk\n\nclass Points(NodeData):\n    def __init__(self, points):\n        self.points = points\n        points_vtk = servermanager.Fetch(points).GetPointData()\n        num_arrays = points_vtk.GetNumberOfArrays()\n        self.array_names = []\n        \n        for i in range(num_arrays):\n            self.array_names.append(points_vtk.GetArrayName(i))\n\n    def __getstate__(self):\n        state = self.__dict__.copy()\n        state[\"points\"] = None\n        return state\n\n    def save(self, dirname):\n        super().save(dirname)\n        SaveData(f\"{dirname}/points.pvd\", self.points)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def load(cls, dirname):\n        base = super().load(dirname)\n        points = PVDReader(FileName=f\"{dirname}/points.pvd\")\n        points.PointArrays = base.array_names\n        base.points = points\n        return base\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"points\"\n\ndef _export_points(points, gt_arrayname, filename, new_arrayname, map, map_name, map_length):\n\n    if filename[-4:] not in [\".vtk\", \".pvd\"]:\n        raise ValueError(\"Currently only VTK legacy data (.vtk) and ParaView data (.pvd) are supported for exporting points.\")\n\n    if len(map) != map_length:\n        raise Exception(f\"The length of {map_name} must be {map_length}\")\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(filename)), exist_ok=True)\n\n    filter = categorical_map_filter(points, gt_arrayname, map, -1, new_arrayname)\n    SaveData(filename, filter)\n\n    Delete(filter)\n\nclass ScalarCriticalPoints(Points):\n\n    def export(self, filename : str, ct_array_name : str = \"CriticalType\", ct_values : List[float] = [0,1,2,3,4]):\n        _export_points(self.points, \"CriticalType\", filename, ct_array_name, ct_values, \"ct_values\", 5)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_export_description(cls):\n        return \"Saves the scalar critical points associated with a node of type scalar_cp.\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_export_param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {\n            \"filename\": \"The filename that should be used for saving the data. The type of file that is produced determines \"\n                        \"the filetype. Use .vtk for legacy VTK files. .pvd for ParaView data files.\",\n            \"ct_array_name\": \"The name of the array that should be used to store the critical types.\",\n            \"ct_values\": \"A list of five numbers that will respectively be stored in the critical types array to indicate \"\n                         \"that a critical point is, respectively, a minimum, 1-saddle, 2-saddle, maximum, or degenerate critical point.\"\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"scalar_cp\"\n    \n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"scalar field critical points\"\n\nclass VectorCriticalPoints(Points):\n\n    def export(self, filename : str, ct_array_name : str = \"CriticalType\", ct_values : List[float] = [0,1,2,3,4,5]):\n        _export_points(self.points, \"CriticalType\", filename, ct_array_name, ct_values, \"ct_values\", 6)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_export_description(cls):\n        return \"Saves the vector critical points associated with a node of type vector_cp.\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_export_param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {\n            \"filename\": \"The filename that should be used for saving the data. The type of file that \"\n                        \"is produced determines the filetype. Use .vtk for legacy VTK files. .pvd for ParaView data files.\",\n            \"ct_array_name\": \"The name of the array that should be used to store the critical types.\",\n            \"ct_values\": \"A list of six numbers that will respectively be stored in the critical types array to indicate \"\n                         \"that a critical point is, respectively, a source, saddle, sink, source spiral, center, and sink spiral.\"\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"vector_cp\"\n    \n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"vector field critical points\"\n\nclass SymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(Points):\n\n    def export(self, filename : str, dp_array_name : str = \"Degeneracy\", dp_values : List[float] = [0,1]):\n        _export_points(self.points, \"CriticalType\", filename, dp_array_name, dp_values, \"dp_values\", 2)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_export_description(cls):\n        return \"Saves the symmetric tensor degenerate points associated with a node of type symmetric_tensor_dp.\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_export_param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {\n            \"filename\": \"The filename that should be used for saving the data. The type of file that is produced determines \"\n                        \"the filetype. Use .vtk for legacy VTK files. .pvd for ParaView data files.\",\n            \"dp_array_name\": \"The name of the array that should be used to store the degeneracy types.\",\n            \"dp_values\": \"A list of two numbers that will respectively be stored in the degeneracy types array to indicate that a \"\n                         \"degenerate point is, respectively, a trisector or wedge.\"\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"symmetric_tensor_dp\"\n    \n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"symmetric tensor field degenerate points\"\n\nclass AsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(Points):\n\n    def export(self, filename : str, dp_array_name : str = \"Degeneracy\", dp_values : List[float] = [0,1]):\n        _export_points(self.points, \"CriticalType\", filename, dp_array_name, dp_values, \"dp_values\", 2)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_export_description(cls):\n        return \"Saves the asymmetric tensor degenerate points associated with a node of type asymmetric_tensor_dp.\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_export_param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {\n            \"filename\": \"The filename that should be used for saving the data. The type of file that is produced determines the filetype. \"\n                        \"Use .vtk for legacy VTK files. .pvd for ParaView data files.\",\n            \"dp_array_name\": \"The name of the array that should be used to store the degeneracy types.\",\n            \"dp_values\": \"A list of two numbers that will respectively be stored in the degeneracy types array to indicate that a \"\n                         \"degenerate point is, respectively, a trisector or wedge.\"\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"asymmetric_tensor_dp\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"asymmetric tensor field degenerate points\"\n\nclass PointsEmbedding(NodeData):\n\n    def __init__(self, points, radius, array_name, lut):\n        self.points = points\n        self.array_name = array_name\n        self.lut = lut\n        self.radius = radius\n\n    def __getstate__(self):\n        state = self.__dict__.copy()\n        state[\"points\"] = None\n        return state\n    \n    def visualize(self, renderView):\n        spheres = ttk.TTKIcospheresFromPoints(Input=self.points)\n        spheres.Radius = self.radius\n\n        display = Show(spheres, renderView, 'GeometryRepresentation')\n\n        lut = GetColorTransferFunction(self.array_name)\n        lut.RGBPoints = self.lut\n        lut.ScalarRangeInitialized = 1.0\n\n        display.LookupTable = lut\n        display.ColorArrayName = ['POINTS', self.array_name]\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"points_embedding\"\n    \nclass ScalarCriticalPointsEmbedding(PointsEmbedding):\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"scalar_cp_embedding\"\n    \n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"scalar field critical points embedding\"\n\nclass VectorCriticalPointsEmbedding(PointsEmbedding):\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"vector_cp_embedding\"\n    \n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"vector field critical points embedding\"\n\nclass SymmetricTensorDegeneratePointsEmbedding(PointsEmbedding):\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"symmetric_tensor_dp_embedding\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"symmetric tensor field degenerate points embedding\"\n\nclass AsymmetricTensorDegeneratePointsEmbedding(PointsEmbedding):\n\n    @classmethod\n    def get_mcp_name(cls):\n        return \"asymmetric_tensor_dp_embedding\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"asymmetric tensor field degenerate points embedding\"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
