{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '240,335p' TOPOPILOT_SCRIPTING_GUIDE.txt && sed -n '1,190p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes/dataLoaders.py && rg -n \\\"class (EmbedSymmetric|ComputeSymmetric|EmbedEigen|SymmetricTensor)\\\" TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes\"","aggregated_output":"\nLoadVectorField(load_path, u_array_name, v_array_name)\n    Loads a 2D vector field from the point arrays holding its x/u and y/v\n    components.\n\nLoadSymmetricTensorField(load_path, A_array_name, B_array_name, D_array_name)\n    Loads a 2D symmetric tensor [[A, B], [B, D]] from three point arrays.\n\nLoadAsymmetricTensorField(load_path, A_array_name, B_array_name,\n                          C_array_name, D_array_name)\n    Loads a 2D general tensor [[A, B], [C, D]] from four point arrays.\n\n\nFIELD EMBEDDINGS\n----------------\n\nEmbedScalarField(parent_node_id, colormap=\"cool warm\")\n    Displays a scalar field as a colored surface (2D) or volume (3D). colormap must\n    be one of the colormap names listed in Section 2.\n\nEmbedVectorField(parent_node_id)\n    Displays a vector field using its geometric vector-field embedding.\n\nEmbedSymmetricTensorField(parent_node_id)\n    Displays a symmetric tensor field using its geometric tensor embedding.\n\nEmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvectorPartition(parent_node_id, resolution=16)\n    Displays the asymmetric-tensor domain partitioned by eigenvector behavior.\n    resolution is the number of subdivisions per grid cell; higher is slower and\n    smoother.\n\nEmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvaluePartition(parent_node_id, resolution=16)\n    Displays regions dominated by scaling, rotation, or anisotropic stretching,\n    including direction where applicable. resolution controls subdivisions per\n    grid cell.\n\n\nSCALAR OPERATIONS AND TOPOLOGICAL STRUCTURES\n--------------------------------------------\n\nPersistenceSimplification(parent_node_id, epsilon)\n    Simplifies a scalar field. epsilon is a fraction of the function range: 0 means\n    no simplification and 1 spans the entire range.\n\nComputePersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id)\n    Computes a scalar field's persistence diagram.\n\nEmbedPersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id, ball_radius=0.02, tube_radius=0.01)\n    Displays persistence pairs as balls and tubes. Both radii are fractions of the\n    scalar function range.\n\nComputeMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n    Computes the Morse-Smale segmentation of a scalar field.\n\nEmbedMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n    Creates displayable geometry for a Morse-Smale segmentation.\n\nComputeIsocontours(parent_node_id, num_contours)\n    Computes num_contours isovalues uniformly across a scalar field's value range.\n\nEmbedIsocontours(parent_node_id, colormap=\"cool warm\", tube_radius=1.0)\n    Displays isocontours with the selected colormap. tube_radius is the contour tube\n    radius used for 2D data.\n\nComputeContourTree(parent_node_id)\n    Computes a scalar field's contour tree.\n\nEmbedContourTree(parent_node_id, ball_radius=3.0, tube_radius=1.5,\n                 color_scheme=[\"#002fff\", \"#758fff\", \"#ffdee7\", \"#ff0046\",\n                               \"#000000\"])\n    Displays contour-tree vertices and edges. ball_radius and tube_radius size the\n    geometry. color_scheme must contain five hex colors for minima, 1-saddles,\n    2-saddles, maxima, and degenerate points, in that order.\n\nComputeMergeTree(parent_node_id, which_tree=\"join\")\n    Computes a merge tree. which_tree must be \"join\" or \"split\".\n\nEmbedMergeTree(parent_node_id, ball_radius=3.0, tube_radius=1.5,\n               color_scheme=[\"#002fff\", \"#758fff\", \"#ffdee7\", \"#ff0046\",\n                             \"#000000\"])\n    Displays merge-tree vertices and edges. Parameters have the same meanings and\n    color order as EmbedContourTree.\n\n\nFIELD-TO-FIELD OPERATIONS\n-------------------------\n\nVectorFieldMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a vector field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nSymmetricTensorMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a symmetric tensor field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nAsymmetricTensorMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts an asymmetric tensor field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nimport vtk\n\nfrom ..types import Scalar, Vector, SymmetricTensor, AsymmetricTensor\nfrom .node import RootNode, ModuleSummary, Guardrail, raise_on_tool_param_false\nfrom topopilot.config import correctness_checks_on\nfrom paraview.simple import *\n\ndef type_guardrail(type_name : str):\n    return Guardrail(f\"ensure that the user actually wants a {type_name} before loading (if it is not clear from the context)\",\n                    f\"explicitly_specified_{type_name.replace(\" \", \"_\")}\",\n                    f\"did the user explicitly specify that they are loading a {type_name}\",\n                    raise_on_tool_param_false(\n                        f\"Cannot create node. The user did not explicitly specify that they are loading a {type_name}.\"\n                    ))\n\nclass LoadScalarField(RootNode):\n\n    def __init__(self, load_path : str, arrayName : str = \"\"):\n        \"\"\"\n        Loads a scalar field from a file given at load_path.\n\n        Args:\n            load_path: The path to the scalar field that should be loaded.\n            arrayName: The name of the array that should be loaded for the scalar field. If this is\n                       left empty and the file only has one array, that single array will be used for the\n                       scalar field.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        super().__init__(load_path, Scalar, locals(), [arrayName])\n\n        reader = vtk.vtkXMLImageDataReader()\n        reader.SetFileName(self.check_file)\n        reader.Update()\n\n        image = reader.GetOutput()\n        pd = image.GetPointData()\n        numArrays = pd.GetNumberOfArrays()\n\n        # if correctness_checks_on():\n        if numArrays == 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} has no arrays\")\n        elif numArrays == 1 and arrayName == \"\":\n            arrayName = pd.GetArrayName(0)\n        elif numArrays > 1:\n            if arrayName == \"\":\n                raise ValueError(f\"The file {load_path} has multiple arrays and the user did not specify one. The user\"\\\n                                \" must specify if the data is scalar, vector, symmetric tensor, or asymmetric tensor data\"\\\n                                \" and which arrays they want to load.\")\n\n            if not pd.HasArray(arrayName):\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} has no array '{arrayName}'\")\n    \n        self.arrayName = arrayName\n        self._commit()\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued loading scalar field\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        return 'Loads a scalar field from a file given at load_path.'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {'load_path': 'The path to the scalar field that should be loaded. Time varying data is loaded by specifying a directory.',\n         'arrayName': 'The name of the array that should be loaded for the scalar field. If '\n                      'this is left empty and the file only has one array, that single array '\n                      'will be used for the scalar field.'}\n\n    def _evaluation_logic(self, filename):\n        vti = XMLImageDataReader(FileName=[filename])\n        vti.PointArrayStatus = [self.arrayName]\n        vti.TimeArray = 'None'\n\n        renameArrays = RenameArrays(Input=vti)\n        renameArrays.PointArrays = [self.arrayName, 'Scalars_']\n        return Scalar(renameArrays)\n\nclass LoadVectorField(RootNode):\n\n    def __init__(self, load_path : str, u_array_name : str, v_array_name : str):\n        \"\"\"\n        Loads a vector field from a file given at load_path.\n\n        Args:\n            load_path: The path to the vector field that should be loaded.\n            u_array_name: The name of the array storing the x component of the vectors.\n            v_array_name: The name of the array storing the y component of the vectors.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        super().__init__(load_path, Vector, locals(), [u_array_name, v_array_name])\n\n        reader = vtk.vtkXMLImageDataReader()\n        reader.SetFileName(self.check_file)\n        reader.Update()\n\n        image = reader.GetOutput()\n        pd = image.GetPointData()\n        numArrays = pd.GetNumberOfArrays()\n\n        if correctness_checks_on():\n            if numArrays < 2:\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} has only {numArrays} arrays, but needs at least 2 to load a vector field.\")\n\n            if not pd.HasArray(u_array_name):\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} has no array '{u_array_name}'\")\n\n            if not pd.HasArray(v_array_name):\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} has no array '{v_array_name}'\")\n        \n            if len(self.dimensions) > 2 and self.dimensions[2] != 1:\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} is three dimensional but currently only 2D vector fields are supported.\")\n\n        self.u_array_name = u_array_name\n        self.v_array_name = v_array_name\n        self._commit()\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued loading vector field\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        return 'Loads a vector field from a file given at load_path.'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {'load_path': 'The path to the vector field that should be loaded. Time varying data is loaded by specifying a directory.',\n         'u_array_name': 'The name of the array storing the x component of the vectors.',\n         'v_array_name': 'The name of the array storing the y component of the vectors.'}\n\n    def _evaluation_logic(self, filename):\n        vti = XMLImageDataReader(FileName=[filename])\n        vti.PointArrayStatus = [self.u_array_name, self.v_array_name]\n        vti.TimeArray = 'None'\n\n        renameArrays = RenameArrays(Input=vti)\n        renameArrays.PointArrays = [self.u_array_name, 'u', self.v_array_name, 'v']\n        return Vector(renameArrays)\n\nclass LoadSymmetricTensorField(RootNode):\n\n    def __init__(self, load_path : str, A_array_name : str, B_array_name : str, D_array_name : str):\n        \"\"\"\n        Loads a 2x2 symmetric tensor field from a file given at load_path.\n\n        Args:\n            load_path: The path to the vector field that should be loaded.\n            A_array_name: The name of the array storing the (1,1) component of the tensors.\n            B_array_name: The name of the array storing the (1,2) component of the tensors.\n                          Since the tensors are symmetric, this also stores the (2,1) component.\n            D_array_name: The name of the array storing the (2,2) component of the tensors.\n        \"\"\"\n\n        super().__init__(load_path, SymmetricTensor, locals(), [A_array_name, B_array_name, D_array_name])\n\n        reader = vtk.vtkXMLImageDataReader()\n        reader.SetFileName(self.check_file)\n        reader.Update()\n\n        image = reader.GetOutput()\n        pd = image.GetPointData()\n        numArrays = pd.GetNumberOfArrays()\n\n        if correctness_checks_on():\n            if numArrays < 3:\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} has only {numArrays} arrays, but needs at least 3 to load a symmetric tensor field.\")\n\n            if not pd.HasArray(A_array_name):\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} has no array '{A_array_name}'\")\n\n            if not pd.HasArray(B_array_name):\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} has no array '{B_array_name}'\")\n        \n            if not pd.HasArray(D_array_name):\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} has no array '{D_array_name}'\")\n\n            if len(self.dimensions) > 2 and self.dimensions[2] != 1:\n                raise ValueError(f\"File {load_path} is three dimensional but currently only 2D symmetric tensor fields are supported.\")\n\n        self.A_array_name = A_array_name\n        self.B_array_name = B_array_name\n        self.D_array_name = D_array_name\n        self._commit()\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued loading symmetric tensor field\"\n\nTopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes/pointNodes.py:145:class ComputeSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(Node):\nTopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes/pointNodes.py:294:class EmbedSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(Node):\nTopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes/fieldVisualizationNodes.py:167:class EmbedSymmetricTensorField(Node):\nTopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes/operations.py:73:class SymmetricTensorMagnitude(Node):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
